# Logitech PRO X SUPERLIGHT (046d:4093 through its 046d:c547 receiver,
# 046d:c094 cabled) -> uaccess on its own hidraw node through the receiver,
# and on its HID++ interface, 02, on its cable.
#
# Not yet checked on this hardware. It is of the G502 X PLUS's generation, on
# the same receiver, so its rules are the X PLUS's hidraw rules in
# 70-g502x.rules, for the same reasons. Through the receiver the mouse's own
# node is matched by its HID device name: a property match would also take
# in the receiver's interfaces, which carry the input of everything paired to
# it. Pair nothing else to this mouse's receiver: going by the kernel's
# hid-logitech-dj.c, a keyboard paired after the mouse could have its
# keystrokes arrive on this node.
#
# The node also carries the keystrokes the mouse sends for a button its
# onboard profile binds to a key, as 70-g502x.rules says of the G502 X PLUS's.
#
# Cabled, its firmware's USB descriptors (version 25.01.B0018) give 00 a boot
# mouse, 01 a keyboard and 02 the vendor collection, the G502 X PLUS's
# layout. Interface 01 is not granted.
#
# No event node is granted: the mouse has no button beyond the five a desktop
# reads, and in host mode Gearbench reads its back and forward through
# HID++ on the hidraw nodes below, and outside host mode none.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:4093.*", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c094", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
